### A. Sign up a second owner (a different person, a different organization)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Second Owner", "email": "second@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026", "organizationName": "Second Estates" }

### B. Log in as owner A  (run this before the requests below)
# @name loginA
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026" }

### C. Log in as owner B
# @name loginB
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "second@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026" }

### 1. No token (expect 401 UNAUTHENTICATED)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/me

### 2. Garbage token (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer abc.def.ghi

### 3. Valid token, A (expect 200 with A's memberships)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4. Org context for A, no header needed (expect 200, role OWNER)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/context
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5. Owner-only route as A (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/owner-only
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6. B names A's organization (expect 403 FORBIDDEN)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/context
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{loginA.response.body.$.memberships[0].organizationId}}

### 7. Malformed organization header (expect 400)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/context
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: not-a-uuid

### 8. B with no header (expect 400 ORGANIZATION_REQUIRED, B has two organizations)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/context
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 9. B as a TENANT in A's organization (expect 200, role TENANT)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/context
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{loginA.response.body.$.memberships[0].organizationId}}

### 10. B tries the owner-only route in A's organization (expect 403, role too low)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/owner-only
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{loginA.response.body.$.memberships[0].organizationId}}

### 11. B on the owner-only route in B's own organization (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/owner-only
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{loginB.response.body.$.memberships[0].organizationId}}

### 12. Log in as A again so the cookie jar holds A's refresh cookie
# @name loginA2
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026" }

### 13. Works now (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA2.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 14. Log out
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/logout

### 15. Same token, still within its 15 minutes (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA2.response.body.$.accessToken}}